  "notes": [
    "ignore-sign is a valid unsigned parser and must VERIFY the coarse parse.int purpose; signed-only near-miss mismatch is checked separately.",
    "Reverse-copy near miss reverses byte order, not the semantically valid direction of copying.",
    "Byte-pair families (memcmp, xor) carry length-prefixed raw payloads; NUL bytes are ordinary data, and keys of length zero make xor a no-op.",
    "Hash transform families carry a native little-endian state word block followed by one 64-byte big-endian message block.",
    "file-read calibration reads the emulator's bounded virtual file probe.dat; the reference writes a NUL terminator and the length out-parameter.",
    "print calibration captures the emulator's bounded stdout; hex32 shapes print one 8-digit hex line for the little-endian first four input bytes."
  ],
